==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|frm|capricieux}}, from {{der|en|it|capriccioso}}, from {{m|it|capriccio}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/kəˈpɹɪʃəs/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-capricious.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-capricious.oga|a=US}}
* {{rhyme|en|ɪʃəs|s=3}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[impulsive|Impulsive]] and [[unpredictable]]; [[determine]]d by [[chance#Noun|chance]], [[impulse]], or [[whim]].
#: {{synonyms|en|arbitrary|whimsical|fickle|flighty|wayward}}
#: {{antonyms|en|conscientious|rigorous}}
#: {{ux|en|I almost died in a '''capricious''' winter storm.}}
#: {{ux|en|Stringent rulers are unlikely to act '''capriciously'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare As You Like It|page=198|scene=iii|act=III|passage=I am heere with thee, and thy Goats, as the moſt '''capricious''' Poet honeſt ''Ouid'' was among Gothes.}}
#* {{RQ:James American|page=11|passage="'''Capricious'''?" And at this monsieur began to laugh. "Oh no, I'm not '''capricious'''. I am very faithful. I am very constant. ''Comprenez''?"}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=25 February 1965|author=w:Civil Aeronautics Board|title=Aircraft Accident Report: Pan American World Airways, Inc Boeing 707-121, N709PA, Near Elkton, Maryland, December 8, 1963|chapter=Analysis|url=https://asn.flightsafety.org/reports/1963/19631208_B701_N709PA.pdf|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20241201161802/https://asn.flightsafety.org/reports/1963/19631208_B701_N709PA.pdf|archivedate=1 December 2024|accessdate=1 December 2024|page=12|text=Although much has been learned about lightning and its effects through research and study, many questions are still unanswered and the upper limits of voltage, current and total energy that may be associated with lightning are not conclusively defined.  The apparent '''capricious''' nature of lightning is evidenced by the range of extremes as well as, in some cases, the unique nature of the damage that results.  Thus, to predict in the absence of physical evidence the exact mechanism of ignition in this particular case is not possible.  By the same reasoning, in view of the known facts of this accident, there is no logical explanation for ignition of the flammable vapors other than some effect stemming directly from the lightning strike.}}

====Usage notes====
* The word ''capricious'' can describe both a person and the decisions which they make.

